IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `lta-core`

-- Land Tax Act 1936 (SA) -- cases for the seat-neutral core (lta-core.l4).
--
-- Expected values worked by hand from the deposited text (the Open Australian Legal Corpus text as at 2023-07-01; not the
-- official text, and out of date), never copied from the encoding's output. Clock for the regulative rules: days.
--
-- THRESHOLDS. Except where the Act states an amount (s 8A(2): 2020/2021 A $450 000 and D $1 350 000; s 8A(3a): D
-- $1 350 000 for 2021/2022 and $2 000 000 for 2022/2023), every threshold below is ASSUMED for the case. None is a
-- gazetted figure.

§ `Cases -- the owner of land (core)`

§§ `ss 2, 4, 9(2), 14-17 -- the owner, the taxing moment, liability`

#ASSERT `the person is an owner of the land` `legal owner`
#ASSERT `the person is an owner of the land` `prospective owner, under a contract to purchase or acquire the land`
#ASSERT `the person is an owner of the land` `occupier of land in a defined shack-site area`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an owner of the land` `mortgagee only`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is an owner of the land` `tenant under an ordinary lease only`)
-- 2024/2025 is calculated at midnight on 30 June 2024; liability arises on 1 July 2024 (s 4(2), (3)).
#ASSERT `the day at whose midnight the land tax is calculated` 2025 EQUALS YMD 2024 6 30
#ASSERT `the day liability for the land tax arises` 2025 EQUALS YMD 2024 7 1
#ASSERT `the person's liability for the land tax on the land` `legal owner` FALSE EQUALS `liable for the land tax on the land`
-- A seller and a buyer under an unsettled contract at midnight on 30 June are both owners, in different capacities.
#ASSERT `the person's liability for the land tax on the land` `prospective owner, under a contract to purchase or acquire the land` TRUE EQUALS `liable, unless the Commissioner treats the owners in another capacity as the sole owners (s 9(2))`
#ASSERT `the person's liability for the land tax on the land` `mortgagee only` TRUE EQUALS `not liable: not an owner of the land at midnight on 30 June before the year`
#ASSERT NOT `a change of ownership during the year relieves the liability for that year`
#ASSERT `each taxpayer can be made to pay all the tax on the land` 2
#ASSERT NOT (`each taxpayer can be made to pay all the tax on the land` 1)
-- s 17(2): a co-owner with a 50% interest who paid $3 501 may recover $1 750.50 from the others.
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable from the other taxpayers` 3501 50 EQUALS 1750.5

§§ `s 5(12) -- the partial exemption scale`

#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 0 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 24.9 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 25 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 30 EQUALS 70
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 50 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 62 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 74.99 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 75 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `the s 5(12) percentage reduction in taxable value for` 75.5 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 5(10)(a), (b), (ba), (bb) -- the home`

GIVEN `ppr` IS A BOOLEAN, `residential` IS A BOOLEAN, `hotel` IS A BOOLEAN, `business` IS A NUMBER, `residence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Home at midnight on 30 June`
`a home` MEANS
    `Home at midnight on 30 June` WITH
        `it is the principal place of residence of a natural person who owns it`                      IS `ppr`
        `the buildings have a predominantly residential character`                                     IS `residential`
        `the buildings are used for a hotel, motel, serviced holiday apartments or similar accommodation` IS `hotel`
        `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`                 IS `business`
        `percentage of the total floor area used as the principal place of residence`                  IS `residence`

-- A home with a study used for a business on 10% of the floor area: wholly exempt under (a).
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 90) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`
-- A shop-front on 40% of the floor area: partially exempt under (b), taxable value reduced by 60% (40% or more but less
-- than 45%).
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 40 60) EQUALS `partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(b)` 60
-- 80% used for business: no residential land exemption.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 80 20) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- Buildings not of a predominantly residential character: none.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 90) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- Not anyone's principal place of residence (a holiday house): none.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- A motel whose owner lives in 80% of the floor area: wholly exempt under (ba).
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE FALSE TRUE 20 80) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ba)`
-- Serviced apartments on 60%, the owner's residence on 40%: (bb), the 60% taken as business area, so 40% off.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE FALSE TRUE 60 40) EQUALS `partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(bb)` 40
-- The owner's residence on 20% of a motel: none.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption for the home` (`a home` TRUE FALSE TRUE 80 20) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- s 7 with s 5(10)(b): a site value of $800 000 reduced by 60% is $320 000; wholly exempt is nil; no exemption is the
-- site value.
#ASSERT `the taxable value of the land` 800000 (`partially exempt under` `s 5(10)(b)` 60) EQUALS 320000
#ASSERT `the taxable value of the land` 800000 (`wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the taxable value of the land` 800000 `no exemption on these grounds` EQUALS 800000

§§ `s 5AA -- a minor interest disregarded`

#ASSERT `the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 3 TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 3 TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 20 TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 20 TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Exactly 50%: prescribed land, but neither s 5AA(2) nor (3) reaches it (finding 3).
#ASSERT NOT (`the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 50 TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 60 TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the resident's interest is disregarded under s 5AA` 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A 3% resident co-owner of a home otherwise wholly exempt under (a): no exemption once the interest is disregarded.
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption after s 5AA` (`a home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100) TRUE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `the residential land exemption after s 5AA` (`a home` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 100) FALSE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`

§§ `s 5(10)(ab), (ac), (ad), (10a), (10b), (11a) -- building work`

GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of building work`
      `ppr before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months after` IS A NUMBER
      `good reasons not to live there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `years already` IS A NUMBER
      `good reasons for longer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `other exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Building work facts`
`building work` MEANS
    `Building work facts` WITH
        `owned by a natural person`                                                          IS TRUE
        `the work`                                                                           IS `kind`
        `it was the owner's principal place of residence immediately before`                IS `ppr before`
        `the buildings were predominantly residential before`                                IS TRUE
        `the buildings will be predominantly residential after the work`                     IS TRUE
        `the owner intends to live there as principal place of residence after the work`     IS TRUE
        `the owner intends to repair or rebuild within 3 years of the destruction`           IS TRUE
        `percentage of the total floor area used for a business or commercial purpose`       IS 0
        `the owner has a residential exemption for other land that is the owner's principal place of residence` IS `other exemption`
        `years the land has already been exempted under this paragraph`                      IS `years already`
        `the Commissioner sees good reasons to exempt for longer than 2 years`               IS `good reasons for longer`
        `months the owner lives there as principal place of residence after completion`      IS `months after`
        `there were good reasons the owner could not live there for 12 months`               IS `good reasons not to live there`
        `rent or other consideration is paid for someone else's occupation`                  IS `rent`

-- Building a new home on vacant land, moving in on completion for at least 12 months: (ad).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)`
-- Lived there only 11 months after completion: not exempt (s 5(10a)(a)(i)) ...
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 11 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- ... unless there were good reasons (s 5(10a)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 11 TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)`
-- Let to someone during the year: not exempt (s 5(10a)(b)).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 12 FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- A third year (2 already exempted): only with the Commissioner's good reasons (s 5(10b)).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE 2 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ad)`
-- Already exempt on another home that is the principal place of residence: not exempt ((ad)(iv)).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner is, or will be, renovating or constructing a building on the land` FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- Moved out of the home to renovate it: (ac); it must have been the principal place of residence.
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner moved out because a building on the land is being renovated or rebuilt` TRUE 12 FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ac)`
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the owner moved out because a building on the land is being renovated or rebuilt` FALSE 12 FALSE FALSE 1 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- A home burnt down: (ab), with no 12-month condition (s 5(10a) names only (ac) and (ad)), for at most 3 years (s 5(11a)).
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(ab)`
#ASSERT `the exemption while the home is destroyed, rebuilt, renovated or built` (`building work` `the home was destroyed or made uninhabitable by an occurrence the owner was not responsible for, or by an accident` TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 3 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
-- s 5(10c), (12a)(e), 5A(4)(c): not more than 5 years after the assessment.
#ASSERT `the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment` (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2029 8 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`the application is made not more than 5 years after the assessment` (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2029 8 2))

§§ `s 5(10)(e), (f), (h), (12a)`

#ASSERT `the retirement village exemption for` `a residential unit occupied under a residence contract by a natural person as principal place of residence` EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(e)`
#ASSERT `the retirement village exemption for` `a facility under the retirement village scheme for the exclusive use of residents and their guests` EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(e)`
#ASSERT `the retirement village exemption for` `other land in the village` EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `it is a retired persons' relocatable home park` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a retired persons' relocatable home park` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the relocatable home park exemption for` TRUE `a site likely to have such a home within the next 12 months` EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(f)`
#ASSERT `the relocatable home park exemption for` FALSE `a site with a relocatable home owned and occupied by a natural person as principal place of residence` EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `the special disability trust exemption` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(h)`
#ASSERT `the special disability trust exemption` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `a s 5(12a) waiver or refund is open to the trustee` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`a s 5(12a) waiver or refund is open to the trustee` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2026 3 1))

§§ `s 5(7), (8) -- telling the Commissioner`

#ASSERT `the days to notify an error in the exemption notice` EQUALS 21
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 5(7) -- notify the Commissioner of an error in the exemption notice within 21 days` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the owner given the exemption notice` `notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy in the exemption notice` 21)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No error in the notice: no duty arises.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 5(7) -- notify the Commissioner of an error in the exemption notice within 21 days` FALSE) 0 EMPTY EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the owner given the exemption notice, "s 5(7): ... maximum penalty $5 000, expiation fee $315" (notified on day 22)
#TRACE `s 5(7) -- notify the Commissioner of an error in the exemption notice within 21 days` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner given the exemption notice` DOES `notify the Commissioner of the error or inaccuracy in the exemption notice` AT 22
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty under s 5(7) or s 5(9)` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the expiation fee under s 5(7) or s 5(9)` EQUALS 315
#ASSERT `the owner must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing under s 5(8)` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the owner must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing under s 5(8)` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing under s 5(8)` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the owner must forthwith inform the Commissioner in writing under s 5(8)` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 5A -- waiver or refund when moving home`

#ASSERT `the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Rent on the old home while both were owned: only if the Commissioner allows otherwise.
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The old home not sold by 30 June: not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 5A(6a): after 3 years of a s 5(10)(ab) exemption on the same land, not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 5A(1)(c) criteria for a new home are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the s 5A(1)(d) criteria for a former home are met` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the s 5A(1)(d) criteria for a former home are met` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

§§ `s 6, s 8A and Schedule 1 -- thresholds and the scale`

-- ASSUMED thresholds for 2024/2025: A $700 000, B $1 100 000, C $1 600 000, D $2 100 000.
`assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` MEANS `Thresholds` OF 700000, 1100000, 1600000, 2100000

-- Clause 3: LT (TB) = $0.50 x 4 000 = $2 000; LT (TC) = $2 000 + $1.00 x 5 000 = $7 000; LT (TD) = $7 000 + $2.00 x 5 000
-- = $17 000.
#ASSERT `LT (TB)` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `LT (TC)` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `LT (TD)` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` EQUALS 17000
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 700000 EQUALS 0
-- $1 over Threshold A is a fractional part of $100: $0.50.
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 700001 EQUALS 0.5
-- $3 950 over A is 40 parts (39 whole and a fraction): $20; $3 900 is 39 parts: $19.50.
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 703950 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 703900 EQUALS 19.5
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 900000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 1100000 EQUALS 2000
-- $150 050 over B is 1 501 parts: $2 000 + $1 501 = $3 501.
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 1250050 EQUALS 3501
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 2000000 EQUALS 15000
-- $400 000 over D: $17 000 + $2.40 x 4 000 = $26 600.
#ASSERT `the land tax on the Schedule 1 Part 2 scale` `the clause 3 rates` `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds` 2500000 EQUALS 26600
-- s 6: under $20 nothing is payable; $20 is.
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 703900 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 703950 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 20
#ASSERT `the land tax on the scale for the year` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 703900 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 19.5

-- 2020/2021 (clause 2): A $450 000 and D $1 350 000 are the Act's own, whatever is supplied; B and C ASSUMED
-- $600 000 and $870 000. LT (TB) = $0.50 x 1 500 = $750; LT (TC) = $750 + $1.25 x 2 700 = $4 125; LT (TD) = $4 125 +
-- $2.00 x 4 800 = $13 725.
`supplied 2020/2021 thresholds` MEANS `Thresholds` OF 500000, 600000, 870000, 1500000
#ASSERT `the thresholds for` 2021 (JUST `supplied 2020/2021 thresholds`) EQUALS JUST (`Thresholds` OF 450000, 600000, 870000, 1350000)
-- $1 000 000: $4 125 + $2.00 x 1 300 = $6 725. $1 500 000: $13 725 + $2.40 x 1 500 = $17 325.
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2021 (JUST `supplied 2020/2021 thresholds`) NOTHING 1000000 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 6725
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2021 (JUST `supplied 2020/2021 thresholds`) NOTHING 1500000 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 17325

-- 2022/2023: D is the Act's $2 000 000 (s 8A(3a)); A, B, C ASSUMED $600 000, $950 000, $1 400 000. LT (TB) = $1 750;
-- LT (TC) = $1 750 + $4 500 = $6 250; LT (TD) = $6 250 + $2.00 x 6 000 = $18 250; $2 200 000: + $2.40 x 2 000 = $23 050.
`supplied 2022/2023 thresholds` MEANS `Thresholds` OF 600000, 950000, 1400000, 1
#ASSERT `the thresholds for` 2023 (JUST `supplied 2022/2023 thresholds`) EQUALS JUST (`Thresholds` OF 600000, 950000, 1400000, 2000000)
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2023 (JUST `supplied 2022/2023 thresholds`) NOTHING 2200000 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 23050
-- 2021/2022: D $1 350 000 (s 8A(3a)).
#ASSERT `threshold D stated by the Act for` 2022 EQUALS JUST 1350000
#ASSERT `threshold D stated by the Act for` 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `threshold A stated by the Act for` 2022 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 8A(8): to the nearest $1 000, $500 up.
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` 1100499 EQUALS 1100000
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest 1000 dollars` 1100500 EQUALS 1101000
-- Supplied unrounded figures: $700 400 goes down to $700 000, $1 099 500 up to $1 100 000.
#ASSERT `the thresholds for` 2025 (JUST (`Thresholds` OF 700400, 1099500, 1600000, 2100000)) EQUALS JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`

-- Not covered: before 2020/2021; no thresholds supplied; thresholds out of order.
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2020 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1000000 EQUALS `not covered` `the assessment year is before 2020/2021: Schedule 1 (inserted from 1 July 2020) has no scale for it, and the earlier scales are not in the deposited text`
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2026 NOTHING NOTHING 1000000 EQUALS `not covered` `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2025 (JUST (`Thresholds` OF 1100000, 700000, 1600000, 2100000)) NOTHING 1000000 EQUALS `not covered` `the thresholds supplied are not in ascending order (Threshold A, B, C, D)`

-- Rates. 2023/2024 is under the deposited clause 3 even if a change is supplied; from 2024/2025 a supplied change is used.
`a supplied change of rates` MEANS `Scale rates` OF 0.50, 1.00, 2.00, 3.00
#ASSERT `the scale rates for` 2022 NOTHING EQUALS `the clause 2 rates`
#ASSERT `the scale rates for` 2024 (JUST `a supplied change of rates`) EQUALS `the clause 3 rates`
#ASSERT `the scale rates for` 2026 NOTHING EQUALS `the clause 3 rates`
-- $2 500 000 in 2025/2026 at a supplied $3.00 over D: $17 000 + $3.00 x 4 000 = $29 000.
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2026 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) (JUST `a supplied change of rates`) 2500000 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 29000

§§ `s 8B -- aggregation and apportionment`

-- A home wholly exempt ($900 000), a rental ($600 000) and a vacant block ($650 050): aggregate $1 250 050, $3 501 in
-- 2024/2025 at the assumed thresholds.
`my parcels` MEANS
    LIST `Parcel` OF 900000, (`wholly exempt under` `s 5(10)(a)`)
         `Parcel` OF 600000, `no exemption on these grounds`
         `Parcel` OF 650050, `no exemption on these grounds`
#ASSERT `the aggregate taxable value of` `my parcels` EQUALS 1250050
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING (`the aggregate taxable value of` `my parcels`) EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 3501
-- Taxed separately, $600 000 and $650 050 would each be under Threshold A: nil. Aggregation costs $3 501.
#ASSERT `the land tax payable for the year` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 650050 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 0
-- s 8B(2): $3 000 over an aggregate of $1 200 000, of which $300 000 is in one assessment: $750 on it.
#ASSERT `the land tax apportioned to the assessment` 3000 300000 1200000 EQUALS 750

§§ `s 5A(3) -- the amount waived or refunded`

-- (a): aggregate $1 250 000 with the new home ($400 000) taxed: $2 000 + $1.00 x 1 500 = $3 500; without it, $850 000:
-- $0.50 x 1 500 = $750. The waiver is $2 750.
#ASSERT `the s 5A(3)(a) waiver or refund` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1250000 400000 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 2750
-- (b): the land alone ($900 000) would bear $1 000; settlement on 18 April 2025 leaves 73 days to 30 June 2025, so
-- $1 000 x 73 / 365 = $200. The refund is the lesser of that and the adjustment paid.
#ASSERT `the s 5A(3)(b) refund of an amount representing land tax` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 900000 250 (YMD 2025 4 18) EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 200
#ASSERT `the s 5A(3)(b) refund of an amount representing land tax` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 900000 150 (YMD 2025 4 18) EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 150
#ASSERT `the s 5A(3)(b) refund of an amount representing land tax` 2026 NOTHING NOTHING 900000 150 (YMD 2026 4 18) EQUALS `not covered` `the thresholds for the assessment year were not supplied: the Commissioner publishes them by Gazette notice (s 8A(7)), and the s 8A(2a), (3) and (3b) formulas are missing from the deposited text`

§§ `s 9 -- more than one owner`

-- Two siblings own a rental at $1 250 050 half each; one also owns $500 000 alone. Joint assessment: $3 501 (s 9(4)).
#ASSERT `the land tax on the joint assessment` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1250050 EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 3501
-- Separate assessment (s 9(6)): $625 025 + $500 000 = $1 125 025; $2 000 + $1.00 x 251 parts = $2 251, less the s 9(8)
-- deduction. The deduction's formula is missing; with an ASSUMED deduction of $1 000 from the notice: $1 251.
#ASSERT `the taxable value on the separate assessment` 50 1250050 500000 0 EQUALS 1125025
#ASSERT `the land tax on the separate assessment` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1125025 (JUST 1000) EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 1251
-- s 9(9): a deduction larger than the tax leaves nil, not a credit.
#ASSERT `the land tax on the separate assessment` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1125025 (JUST 3000) EQUALS `the land tax, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the land tax on the separate assessment` 2025 (JUST `assumed 2024/2025 thresholds`) NOTHING 1125025 NOTHING EQUALS `not covered` `the s 9(8) deduction was not supplied: its formula is missing from the deposited text`

§§ `s 19 -- paying, and tax defaults`

#ASSERT `the days to pay land tax after service of the assessment` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 19(1) -- pay the land tax within 30 days after service of the assessment` 3501) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` (`pay the land tax specified in the assessment` 3501) 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A part payment does not count; the full amount on day 25 does.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 19(1) -- pay the land tax within 30 days after service of the assessment` 3501) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` (`pay the land tax specified in the assessment` 3000) 10), (EVENT `the taxpayer` (`pay the land tax specified in the assessment` 3501) 25)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 19(1): land tax must be paid within 30 days ..." (only $3 000 of $3 501 paid)
#TRACE `s 19(1) -- pay the land tax within 30 days after service of the assessment` 3501 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `pay the land tax specified in the assessment` 3000 AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- With TAA s 91: paid on day 20, objected on day 40, objection allowed in full on day 100.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 19(1) with TAA s 91 -- pay within 30 days even while objecting` 3501 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` (`pay the land tax specified in the assessment` 3501) 20), (EVENT `the objector` `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister, stating the grounds fully and in detail` 40), (EVENT `the Minister` (`give written notice of the determination of the objection, with reasons` `the objection is allowed in full`) 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 19(1): ..." (objected on day 10 but did not pay: the objection does not suspend payment)
#TRACE `s 19(1) with TAA s 91 -- pay within 30 days even while objecting` 3501 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the objector` DOES `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister, stating the grounds fully and in detail` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
#ASSERT `there is a tax default under s 19(2)` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`there is a tax default under s 19(2)` TRUE FALSE)
